[{"_1":2,"_3":4},"root",{"_5":84},"routes/item",{"_5":6},"data",{"_7":8,"_9":10},"item",{"_11":12,"_13":14,"_15":16,"_17":18,"_19":-5,"_20":21,"_22":23,"_24":25,"_26":27,"_28":27,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":-5,"_40":-5,"_41":42,"_43":44,"_45":46,"_47":48,"_49":50,"_51":52,"_53":36,"_54":55,"_56":-5,"_57":36,"_58":59},"expiresAt",1794962440000,"id","j5ze1ckk5wgmksuh1g4a9adez","title","Apple 服务与 NSA 网络中断，Equinor 确认遭网络攻击","originalTitle","Apple Services Disrupted as NSA Network Goes Down and Equinor Faces Cyberattack","summary","Apple 因内部更新导致 iCloud 账户登录、App Store、Apple Music 和 AppleCare on Device 等服务中断，Apple 表示多数系统已恢复；NSA 涉密通信网络 NSANet 也发生中断，但无证据显示由网络攻击引起。","reason","source",{"_65":83},"links",{"_59":82},"publishedAt","2026-11-17T20:52:24.000Z","discoveredAt","2026-11-17T22:25:38.259Z","timelineAt","category","activity","tags",[66,68,81],"score",43,"selected",false,"channel","news","story","x","readingMode","full","author","Pierluigi Paganini","body",{"_77":-5,"_59":78,"_79":-5,"_80":36},"outline",[71],"relatedStories",[],"topics",[60,61,62],"indexable","markdownAvailable",true,"group","hasTranslation","bodyLanguage","original",{"_63":69,"_65":70},{"_63":67,"_65":68},{"_63":64,"_65":66},"slug","attack","name","攻击活动","incident","应急响应","apple","Apple / 苹果",{"_11":72,"_73":74,"_75":76},"sec-1","text","Apple and NSA services faced outages as Equinor reported a cyberattack, highligh","level",2,"zh","<h2 id=\"sec-1\">Apple and NSA services faced outages as Equinor reported a cyberattack, highlighting the risks facing increasingly connected infrastructure.</h2><p>Apple customers faced widespread service problems on November 17, with issues affecting iCloud, the App Store, Apple Music and AppleCare on Device. </p><figure><a href=\"https://i0.wp.com/securityaffairs.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/11/image-45.png?ssl=1\"><img width=\"1024\" height=\"476\" src=\"/dailyinfo/media/e81a16c748c0cefb.webp\" srcset=\"/dailyinfo/media/7969c127e4ba49be.webp 720w, /dailyinfo/media/c4972352f8eaa5c1.webp 1200w, /dailyinfo/media/e81a16c748c0cefb.webp 1600w\" sizes=\"(min-width: 1536px) 760px, (min-width: 1024px) calc(100vw - 524px), (min-width: 640px) 608px, calc(100vw - 32px)\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" alt=\"\"></a></figure><p>The disruption came after a week of technical failures involving major technology companies, <a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/203272/security/u-s-banks-struggle-with-outages-amid-wider-technology-disruptions.html\">banking services</a> and US government networks. At the same time, Norwegian energy company Equinor <a href=\"https://www.reuters.com/technology/equinor-detects-cyberattack-against-some-it-systems-2026-11-17/\">disclosed</a> a cyberattack against some of its IT systems.</p><p>Apple’s System <a href=\"https://www.apple.com/support/systemstatus/\">Status page</a> reported problems with iCloud Account and Sign In, affecting all users. The issue prevented customers from signing in to their Apple accounts or caused repeated requests for their Apple ID passwords. Some users also reported difficulties activating new iPhones, suggesting that the disruption was affecting essential account services, not just individual apps.</p><p><a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/11/17/apple-services-including-icloud-app-store-and-apple-music-hit-by-outage/\">According to TechCrunch</a>, the problems also affected the App Store, Apple Music and AppleCare on Device. Apple had not issued a detailed public explanation at the time of publication, beyond listing the incidents on its status page. The company said in a statement that the issue was caused by an internal update.</p><p><em>“Many of our systems are back up and running after an internal update caused some outages this morning,” reads the <a href=\"https://www.nytimes.com/2026/11/17/technology/apple-down-outage-issues.html\">statement</a>. “We’re working to get the remaining systems online as soon as possible.”</em></p><p>The Apple outage attracted attention because it followed several other major disruptions. Microsoft <a href=\"https://securityaffairs.com/202932/security/microsoft-cloud-outage-hits-outlook-teams-copilot-and-ai-services.html\">had experienced a widespread failure</a> affecting Outlook and Teams, while JPMorgan Chase customers had reported problems with online banking. A separate outage also affected the National Security Agency’s classified internal communications network, known as NSANet.</p><p>The NSA incident raised particular concerns because the network supports classified communications. However, the cause and full extent of the disruption remained unclear. Reports cited by <a href=\"https://www.forbesmiddleeast.com/innovation/cybersecurity/nsa-network-apple-services-hit-by-outages-as-equinor-reports-cyberattack\">Forbes Middle East</a> said there was no evidence that the NSA outage resulted from a cyberattack. A system patch had reportedly been underway before the disruption.</p><p>The growing number of outages does not mean they share the same cause or are part of a coordinated cyber campaign. Technical problems, software bugs, configuration errors and infrastructure failures can affect major services without any cyberattack. Claims about AI-powered attacks should not be made without evidence.</p><p>On the same day, Norway’s energy company Equinor reported a cyberattack against some of its IT systems. The company said the attack had not affected its operations or production, and it had found no evidence of data theft. Equinor said it had activated its response teams and notified the relevant authorities. The company stated that “there were no signs data had been stolen.”</p><p>The Equinor incident added a confirmed cyberattack to a day already marked by several service outages. However, these events should not be confused. Equinor confirmed a cyberattack, while there was no evidence that the outages affecting Apple and the NSA were caused by malicious activity.</p><p>Cyberattacks can compromise systems and data, while ordinary technical failures can disrupt services that businesses, public institutions and millions of people depend on. Both require effective incident response, clear communication and the ability to maintain essential operations when technology fails.</p><p>For now, there is no evidence that the recent outages affecting Apple, Microsoft, the NSA, banks and aviation systems are connected. Nor should every major service disruption be treated as evidence of a cyberattack. As Forbes reported about the NSA incident, “there was no evidence the disruption was the result of a cyberattack.”</p><p>The distinction matters. In a period of heightened cyber threats and growing dependence on digital services, organizations need to investigate incidents carefully, communicate what they know and avoid confusing coincidence with attribution. A technical outage is not necessarily a cyberattack, but it can still expose serious weaknesses in the systems on which society depends.</p><p><strong>Follow me on Twitter:&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://twitter.com/securityaffairs\"><strong>@securityaffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://www.facebook.com/sec.affairs\"><strong>Facebook</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;and&nbsp;</strong><a href=\"https://infosec.exchange/@securityaffairs\"><strong>Mastodon</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><a href=\"http://www.linkedin.com/pub/pierluigi-paganini/b/742/559\"><strong>Pierluigi&nbsp;Paganini</strong></a><strong></strong></p><p><strong>(</strong><a href=\"http://securityaffairs.co/wordpress/\"><strong>SecurityAffairs</strong></a><strong>&nbsp;–&nbsp;hacking,&nbsp;Apple)</strong></p>","zhKind","complete","Apple","https://securityaffairs.com/203354/security/apple-outages-add-to-growing-concerns-over-technology-service-disruptions.html","Security Affairs",{"_85":86,"_87":-5},"changelogVersion","2026-10-01T08:00","release"]
